A||||7||WisconsinGT||What would you do if....||||1||
Z||000000||WisconsinGT||08-23-2000||01:21 AM||||you had a brand new Fiero Auto. Shift Counsle and you wanted to reinforce it so you did not have to worry about the seperation that happens over years of use?  ||||reg||1
Z||000001||mrfiero||08-23-2000||02:06 AM||||I'd have to say that there is little you can really do without risking damage to a new console.  I know I wouldn't mess around with a new console....those things are impossible to find! <P>I always use a sunshade in the windshield when parked and I lay a hand towel over the console too.  This at least minimizes the suns damage.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||08-23-2000||12:32 PM||||I've got the gray interior in a black car..... If you don't use the sunshade in the thing you usually regret it about the time you grab the steering wheel.<P>Those reflective bubble wrap type ones are the ones I like. About $6 and they are washable. I've had the one I've got for over a year. Those cardboard jobs stink and cost almost as much. The springy fabric ones are a pain to roll up.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Monkeyman||08-23-2000||05:34 PM||||Ditto what Ogre said, but...even if you have to cut a piece of cardboard to fit your windshield while you save up the $6, do it.  I have a dark purple car with the gray interior.  Probably not as bad as black, but bad enough.  I haven't gotten around to getting a sunshade (and usually work nights anyhow), but that'll be one of the 1st things I get once I start days (probably next week).||||reg||1
Z||000004||WisconsinGT||08-24-2000||12:28 PM||||Thanks guys. But I was thinking of the underside. Could I put something in the weak areas like glue (Shoe Goo) to reinforce this thing. I have a brand new Shift Counsle. Any other ideas? Thnaks.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Monkeyman||08-24-2000||01:08 PM||||Now I'm getting a little confused.  Exactly what are you trying to reinforce?||||reg||1
Z||000006||HugGRRRFiero||08-24-2000||01:45 PM||||Are you trying to reinforce around the top edge?  <P>Yea, you could use some clear automotive GOOP around the top edges of the console where you won't be able to see it because it's under the shift plate.  I'd let the stuff dry before putting it back in the car and the shifter plate.<P>I wouldn't try to pull up the edge to get the goop under the edge though.  If it's not broken, don't fix it...<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/huggrrr.gif">  <BR>  <A HREF="mailto:HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com">HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||DXR_DAD||08-24-2000||09:16 PM||||I think your on the right track with the glue BUT!!! you would need to glue the shifter plate to the housing (NOT GOOD) if the plate were to break, get scratched and need to be replaced.<P>I'll go with mrfiero on this one. Don't mess with, just take care of it. I've done a re-glue job on three center consoles in the last month!! good shifter consoles are hard to find!!<P>DXR_DAD||||reg||5
